{"name":"French Wine","hex":"#ac1e44","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"french","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare food by cutting it into strips.","To kiss (another person) while inserting one’s tongue into the other person's mouth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/french"},{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"French wine","blocks":[{"text":"French wine is produced throughout all of France in quantities between 50 and 60 million hectolitres per year, or 7–8 billion bottles. France is one of the largest wine producers in the world. French wine traces its history to the 6th century BCE, with many of France's regions dating their wine-making history to Roman times. The wines produced range from expensive wines sold internationally to modest wines usually only seen within France such as the Margnat wines of the post-war period."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/French_taste_of_wines.JPG/330px-French_taste_of_wines.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_wine"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg/500px-A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg/1280px-A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg/500px-A_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_%287309839432%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vineyards in Vosne-Romanée in Burgundy, a village that is the source of some of France's most expensive wines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_vineyard_worker_manually_tills_the_soil_near_Vosne-Roman%C3%A9e_in_Burgundy_(7309839432).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Chateau_Pichon-Longueville_Baron_01.jpg/500px-Chateau_Pichon-Longueville_Baron_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co